+  <section class="clip" id="beat-11" data-beat-id="beat-11" data-track-index="0" data-start="179.1" data-duration="13.65"><div class="kicker">ORDER MATTERS</div><div class="order"><div class="step"><span>FIRST</span>Let go</div><div class="step"><span>THEN</span>Carry forward</div></div><p class="sub">Otherwise, an inventory becomes a defense.</p><p class="narration">But we do the letting-go work first. Not the other way around. Because if you build your carry-forward list while you're still holding on to everything, the list stops being useful. It becomes a defense.</p></section>
+  <section class="clip" id="beat-12" data-beat-id="beat-12" data-track-index="0" data-start="192.75" data-duration="6.45"><div class="kicker">TWO EXERCISES · ONE ORDER</div><div class="equation"><div class="pill">LET GO</div><div class="plus">→</div><div class="pill">CARRY FORWARD</div></div><p class="narration">Two exercises. Both matter. Let's do them in the right order.</p></section>
